Looking at this problem, I need to prove:
```
K.Drop(K.Put(K.Put(m,k,x),j,y),k) == (if k == j then K.Drop(m,k) else K.Put(K.Drop(m,k),j,y))
```

The functions `Put` and `Drop` are opaque, so I need to use the provided lemmas to reason about their keys and values.

Let me analyze the two cases:

**Case k == j:**
- LHS: `K.Drop(K.Put(K.Put(m,k,x),k,y),k)` - Put x at k, then put y at k (overwriting), then drop k
- RHS: `K.Drop(m,k)` - Just drop k from m
- These should be equal since dropping k removes everything we added at k

**Case k != j:**
- LHS: `K.Drop(K.Put(K.Put(m,k,x),j,y),k)` - Put x at k, put y at j, drop k
- RHS: `K.Put(K.Drop(m,k),j,y)` - Drop k from m, then put y at j
- These should be equal since the operations on different keys commute

I need to prove equality of maps by showing they have the same keys and same values at each key.

Let me build the proof using the available lemmas:

1. `O1.PutKeys(m, k, v)` - gives us keys of Put
2. `O1.DropKeys(m, k)` - gives us keys of Drop  
3. `O2.PutAt(m, k, v, q)` - gives us values in Put at position q
4. `O2.DropAt(m, k, q)` - gives us values in Drop at position q
5. `A.Equal(a, b)` - proves map equality from matching keys and values

```json
{"HelperA.dfy": "var lhs := K.Drop(K.Put(K.Put(m,k,x),j,y),k);
    var inner := K.Put(m,k,x);
    var outer := K.Put(inner,j,y);
    O1.PutKeys(m,k,x);
    O1.PutKeys(inner,j,y);
    O1.DropKeys(outer,k);
    O1.DropKeys(m,k);
    if k == j {
      var rhs := K.Drop(m,k);
      assert lhs.Keys == rhs.Keys;
      forall q | q in lhs ensures q in rhs && lhs[q] == rhs[q] {
        O2.DropAt(outer,k,q);
        O2.DropAt(m,k,q);
        if q == j {
          O2.PutAt(inner,j,y,q);
          O2.PutAt(m,k,x,q);
        } else {
          O2.PutAt(inner,j,y,q);
          O2.PutAt(m,k,x,q);
        }
      }
      A.Equal(lhs, rhs);
    } else {
      var rhs := K.Put(K.Drop(m,k),j,y);
      var dm := K.Drop(m,k);
      O1.PutKeys(dm,j,y);
      assert lhs.Keys == rhs.Keys;
      forall q | q in lhs ensures q in rhs && lhs[q] == rhs[q] {
        O2.DropAt(outer,k,q);
        if q == j {
          O2.PutAt(inner,j,y,q);
          O2.PutAt(dm,j,y,q);
        } else {
          O2.PutAt(inner,j,y,q);
          O2.PutAt(dm,j,y,q);
          O2.DropAt(m,k,q);
          if q in m {
            O2.PutAt(m,k,x,q);
          }
        }
      }
      A.Equal(lhs, rhs);
    }"}
```

